<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kraków</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1525">1525</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Cracow · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-teutonic-war-1519-1521">Polish–Teutonic War (1519–1521)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> of 8 April 1525 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-teutonic-war-1519-1521">Polish–Teutonic War</a> of 1519–1521. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia">Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, secularised the order's state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and turned it into the hereditary Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a>, a fief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a>. Two days later he paid homage to his uncle, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old">Sigismund I the Old</a>, in Kraków's market square.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-krakow.jpg" alt="Treaty of Kraków" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Traktat_krakowski_zawarty_mi%C4%99dzy_Zygmuntem_I_Starym_a_Albrechtem_Hohenzollernem_(003)_-_756_Perg._-_Czartoryski_Library_in_Krak%C3%B3w.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
